message: "If you use RecursiveCal or build on its software or synthetic experiments, please cite this work and record the exact commit used."
title: "RecursiveCal: Reproducible Active Calibration and a Software-in-the-Loop Workbench"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Venkateshwar Reddy"
    family-names: "Jambula"
    website: "https://github.com/Venkat-RJ"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Venkat-RJ/RecursiveCal"
url: "https://github.com/Venkat-RJ/RecursiveCal"
abstract: "An open source research workbench for synthetic active diagnosis and calibration, with a persistent SI liftgate rig, an observation-only Bayesian investigator, independent calibration verification, CAD replay, measured-data import, preserved contextual-bandit experiments, and explicit model-adequacy limits."
keywords:
  - calibration
  - experimental design
  - system identification
  - software in the loop
  - contextual bandits
